WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.610
Hey, welcome back to 40 Days of Holiness.

2
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.620
Today, I want to encourage you to grab a hold of a workbook, and we're

3
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.640
going to talk about what holiness means.

4
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.360
The Bible is full of pictures. It gives lots of

5
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.380
metaphors. It's not primarily a definitions book or

6
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.600
a philosophical meanderings book. Jesus told parables.

7
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.550
He told picture stories. God gives us word pictures.

8
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.140
And for the next 10 days, I'm going to focus on a lot of the

9
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.170
positive statements, the metaphors, the pictures of what it means

10
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:40.840
to be holy.

11
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.580
Now, the other day we said it's more than subtraction.

12
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.540
Today, we're starting with the positive pictures of what it does mean.

13
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.800
Today's theme is Holiness Means Loving God With All Your Heart.

14
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.000
Matthew 22:36 says this: "Teacher, which

15
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.940
is the greatest commandment in the law?" And Jesus replied, "Love the Lord your God

16
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.980
with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your mind.

17
00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:06.100
This is the first and greatest commandment.

18
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.820
And the second one is like it, love your neighbor as yourself.

19
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.900
All the Law and the Prophets hang

20
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.060
on these two commands."

21
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.480
Jesus, in response to this question, gives

22
00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.280
us the idea that loving God is the

23
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.220
first and the most important, the most comprehensive

24
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.120
command in all of scripture. Every other command flows

25
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.500
out of it and depends on this one.

26
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.200
Now, this is important at this moment that we take a moment and recognize what

27
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:40.900
it means

28
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.860
to love God. Because we only have one word for love in English, and it has this

29
00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.860
huge range of intensity, right? I love pizza and I love my wife.

30
00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.160
I love my phone and I love Jesus.

31
00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.060
And those two are not the same, right?

32
00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.520
John Wesley gives what I think is probably the best definition that I've ever heard

33
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.540
of loving God with all of our heart.

34
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.930
Here's what he says: "What is it to love God, but to delight in him,

35
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.140
to rejoice in his will,

36
00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.580
to desire continually to please him, to

37
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.620
seek and find our happiness in him, and to

38
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.440
thirst day and night for a fuller enjoyment of

39
00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:22.680
him?"

40
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.660
That is marvelous, isn't it? All Christians agree that this is

41
00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.520
the primary thing, and all Christians also agree that this is hard,

42
00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.240
even after we're saved. Why is that? Here's why.

43
00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:39.240
Because our heart is still divided.

44
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.920
This is clear enough from scripture and from experience.

45
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.220
And remember when we said a few days ago that you were going to need to put on

46
00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.080
your possibility glasses instead of your depravity glasses to read the scripture?

47
00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.360
Right? This is where you're going to need them.

48
00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:58.280
You're going to need to put on the right set of glasses because here's what

49
00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.260
most Christians do with this. "Well, there's one more command

50
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.130
I'll never be able to keep till I get to heaven." Right?

51
00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.370
"I guess I'm never going to be able to do that.

52
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.820
Can't love the Lord with all my heart."

53
00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.900
You recognize that, right? It's depravity glasses.

54
00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.020
It's reading the commandments of God with exactly the same

55
00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.080
attitude and exactly the same amount of hope as a non-Christian who wishes they

56
00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.680
could do right, but can't.

57
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.500
It is my conviction that if Jesus commands us to love him with

58
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.420
all of our heart, that he was, are you ready?

59
00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.020
Completely sincere and willing to grant the power to

60
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:35.260
do it.

61
00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.049
Not through our teeth-gritting self-control, but through the power of

62
00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.280
the indwelling, purifying Holy Spirit's work.

63
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.600
So here's a beautiful thing I want you to believe.

64
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.640
The greatest assurance you can do something is that God has

65
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.220
asked it of you.

66
00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.060
If we look at that verse with these glasses, we would say, "Oh,

67
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.080
look at the possibilities of grace.

68
00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.660
Look what's been granted to God's children by their Father."

69
00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.840
The world and the flesh and the devil are

70
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.900
constantly raising up other things to tempt us to place our love

71
00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.620
upon them, things we would call them idols, idolatry.

72
00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.190
And holiness means rejecting those idols offered by the world,

73
00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.340
the flesh, and the devil, and keeping our love fixed

74
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.200
upon Christ. It means a heart that is whole and

75
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:25.960
undivided.

76
00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.800
My friend, Dr. Phil Brown says, "Our creator, who knows our design

77
00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:34.120
and empowers our inner life, will not command the

78
00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:34.840
impossible."

79
00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.460
That's beautiful. See, that's why we can get here to loving God with

80
00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.380
all our heart, because the whole Trinity is involved in creating holiness

81
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.360
in you. As the Father, he wills it in eternity past, Ephesians

82
00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.150
1, right? As the Son, he provides it on the cross, Hebrews

83
00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.740
13. As the Spirit, he executes it from

84
00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.099
within our hearts. Oh my goodness, so many scriptures.

85
00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:58.940
So

86
00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.740
what does this mean? Does this mean I'm never going to mess up?

87
00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.880
Loving God with all your heart means that there's no problems? Well, no.

88
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.920
Wholehearted love,

89
00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.740
it affects performance, but it's not the same thing as perfect performance.

90
00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.800
Let me give you a quick illustration that my dad told me one time.

91
00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:21.140
My dad was out washing the 40-foot travel trailer

92
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.720
that we had. He was washing it. We were living in it at the time,

93
00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.320
and he was up on a ladder in like 85-degree

94
00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.880
weather and was washing and waxing the trailer.

95
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.760
My little sister, who was, oh, probably five at the

96
00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.890
time, had been out playing on the church grounds,

97
00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:44.760
and she had gone and played in the church bus, and she was coming back,

98
00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:49.060
and she had found, he didn't know, but she had found a cup in the church bus.

99
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.960
And she was carrying that cup, and she went inside the house and got some ice in it

100
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.810
and put some water in it, and she came back out of the trailer,

101
00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:00.430
and she looked up, and she saw her daddy, and he was waxing the trailer

102
00:06:01.472 --> 00:06:04.232
And she said to him, "Daddy, would you like a drink?"

103
00:06:05.112 --> 00:06:08.832
And he said, "I sure would." So he climbed down off the ladder,

104
00:06:09.432 --> 00:06:13.232
reached over, and she, with sparkling eyes and happy face,

105
00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:17.192
she handed him the water. And he said, "I took it, and just as I began to raise

106
00:06:17.212 --> 00:06:19.212
it to my lips, I looked down inside it."

107
00:06:20.272 --> 00:06:23.932
And he said, "I don't know what it was floating in there, but

108
00:06:24.072 --> 00:06:26.772
something wasn't right with this glass of water."

109
00:06:27.732 --> 00:06:30.912
And he said, "But at that moment," he said, "I had a couple of choices.

110
00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:32.792
I could say, 'I don't want your water.

111
00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:34.592
If you can't do better than that, I don't want it.

112
00:06:34.752 --> 00:06:35.712
Bring me some clean water.'"

113
00:06:36.992 --> 00:06:37.842
But he said, "Instead,

114
00:06:38.732 --> 00:06:42.492
I looked down into it, and I looked past, and I saw the

115
00:06:42.592 --> 00:06:45.561
sparkling eyes of a little girl who wanted nothing

116
00:06:45.592 --> 00:06:47.772
more than just to please her dad,

117
00:06:48.952 --> 00:06:49.772
just to make him happy,

118
00:06:50.692 --> 00:06:51.592
and just to give him a drink."

119
00:06:52.892 --> 00:06:56.432
And he said, "I saw past imperfect performance,

120
00:06:57.252 --> 00:06:58.952
and I saw pure motive."

121
00:07:01.132 --> 00:07:02.532
What God wants to give you

122
00:07:03.392 --> 00:07:07.232
is not something that will always create perfect performance in you.

123
00:07:08.212 --> 00:07:10.942
Instead, what he wants to do is give you such a

124
00:07:11.252 --> 00:07:14.612
participation in the inner life of the Trinity

125
00:07:15.512 --> 00:07:19.472
that your motivation is purified to love him with all your

126
00:07:19.512 --> 00:07:19.812
heart.

127
00:07:21.232 --> 00:07:24.512
So that your motivation is purified to

128
00:07:24.572 --> 00:07:28.392
be a desire to continually please him,

129
00:07:28.592 --> 00:07:32.322
seek and find our happiness in him, thirst day and night for a fuller enjoyment of

130
00:07:32.352 --> 00:07:32.512
him.

131
00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:37.232
And so that's what we're aiming for. That's what we're trying for.

132
00:07:37.592 --> 00:07:40.992
That's what we're headed toward. So tomorrow, we're going to continue talking about

133
00:07:41.032 --> 00:07:44.712
how God produces that in our hearts.

134
00:07:45.202 --> 00:07:49.102
That's the first metaphor, the first word picture that the Bible gives us

135
00:07:49.212 --> 00:07:52.412
of holiness, loving God with all your heart.

136
00:07:52.912 --> 00:07:53.752
See you back here tomorrow.
